🌑 SCENE 5-A-1｜The Day He Fell

TORONTO DOWNTOWN - DAY

The Protagonist (Middle_Lead) walks down a busy avenue after being discharged from a psychiatric ward.
Cars stream endlessly through the streets.

Voices of strangers.
The sound of traffic signals.
The rhythm of everyday city life.
Yet the scenery overlaps with the memories inside his mind.

Heavy steel doors.
White hospital rooms.
Fragments of the past.
Flashbacks.

His vision begins to tremble.
His breathing becomes uneven.

Then—
His body collapses.
He falls onto the pavement.

His face strikes the ground hard.
For several moments, he cannot move.

Blood begins to flow from his mouth.
People gather around him.

PASSERBY
“Are you alright?”

ANOTHER PASSERBY
“Should we call an ambulance?”

Middle_Lead cannot fully understand what has happened.

He stares only at the blood.

Slowly, he rises to his feet.

Middle_Lead
“I'm alright.
I can get home on my own.”

He thanks the people around him.

Then he starts walking again.

---------------------------------------

🌑 SCENE 5-A-2｜The Warmth of Reunion

TORONTO STREET - CONTINUOUS

Middle_Lead walks while holding a hand against the bleeding wound.

Then—
A man suddenly stops in front of him.

Pure_Friend_midterm.
An old friend.

Pure_Friend_midterm
“...Is that really you?”

Middle_Lead stops walking.

Pure_Friend_midterm
“I've been worried about you for a long time.
What happened?”

Middle_Lead searches for words.

But none come.

Middle_Lead
“I don't know.
Even now...
I don't really understand it myself.”

His friend nods quietly.

Pure_Friend_midterm
“Go home and rest.
We'll talk another day.”

They exchange contact information.

For the first time in a very long while,
Middle_Lead feels the warmth of human connection.

FADE OUT.

